   "id": "err-a11",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The labels a<sub>11</sub> … a<sub>23</sub> count rows and columns from 1, but a C array counts from 0: <code>int a[2][3]</code> holds <code>a[0][0]</code>, <code>a[0][1]</code>, <code>a[0][2]</code>, <code>a[1][0]</code>, <code>a[1][1]</code>, <code>a[1][2]</code>, stored in that order."
  },
  {
   "id": "err-rotate",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "As printed, the index set ends at $\\mathrm{length}(a)$; the last index of $a$ is $\\mathrm{length}(a) - 1$, so $i$ runs over $\\{0,\\ldots,\\mathrm{length}(a)-1\\}$."
  },
  {
   "id": "wp-array-fn-5",
   "kind": "book",
